BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Love & Information at Napa Valley College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
UID:260424_nZ0jpbt1ECkNxyShfjMPw
DESCRIPTION:Written by Caryl Churchill\, this play explores the complexiti
 es of human connection in the information age. The story delves into them
 es of love\, knowledge\, and identity\, presenting a kaleidoscope of conte
 mporary human experiences. In a world saturated with texts\, headlines\, 
 data\, and digital noise\, Churchill’s daring work asks a simple but urg
 ent question: how do we truly connect? \n\nChurchill's sharp dialogue and
  minimalist style create a sense of urgency\, prompting audiences to refle
 ct on how they process information and form connections in an increasingly
  digital world. \n\nDirected by Olivia Cowell & Jennifer King.
LOCATION:Napa Valley College
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/love-information/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Love & Information
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
UID:2604246Ad2sk6RsEux-NxIIb38aQ
DESCRIPTION:Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center (PAC) presents Love
  & Information\, the electrifying contemporary play by celebrated playwrig
 ht Caryl Churchill. In a world saturated with texts\, headlines\, data\, 
 and digital noise\, Churchill’s daring work asks a simple but urgent que
 stion: how do we truly connect? \n\nFast-moving\, surprising\, and deeply
  human\, Love & Information unfolds through a kaleidoscope of short\, vivi
 d scenes. Moments of intimacy collide with flashes of humor\, anxiety\, cu
 riosity\, and longing as characters search for meaning in an age of cons
 tant communication. A confession\, a secret\, a scientific discovery\, a m
 emory—each scene reveals how love\, knowledge\, and identity shape our l
 ives. \n\nChurchill’s razor-sharp writing invites audiences to piece to
 gether the story themselves\, discovering connections between moments that
  are by turns funny\, unsettling\, tender\, and profound. The result is a 
 theatrical experience that mirrors the rhythm of modern life—fragmented\
 , immediate\, and emotionally resonant. \n\n“Love & Information captur
 es the speed and complexity of contemporary life while revealing the deep 
 human longing for connection beneath it\,” said co-directors Jennifer 
 King and Olivia Cowell. “The play challenges actors to move quickly betw
 een characters\, ideas\, and emotional worlds\, and our student ensemble e
 mbraces that challenge with imagination and precision.” \n\nThe product
 ion is co-directed by Jennifer King\, Napa Valley College Theater Arts Dep
 artment Coordinator/Artistic Director and professional stage director\, an
 d Olivia Cowell\, Napa Valley College Theater and Film Studies Instructor 
 and Executive Director of Cafeteria Kids Theater. Both are leaders of Shak
 espeare Napa Valley and bring a shared commitment to dynamic ensemble stor
 ytelling to the production. \n\nLove & Information will be performed in t
 he intimate Studio Theater of the Napa Valley College Performing Arts Cent
 er\, placing audiences just steps away from the actors and immersing them 
 in the immediacy of Churchill’s theatrical world. With only six performa
 nces\, seating is limited and audiences are encouraged to secure tickets
  early by visiting www.performingartnapavalley. \n\nInventive\, provocat
 ive\, and surprisingly moving\, Love & Information showcases the versati
 lity of Napa Valley College’s student performers while inviting audience
 s to reflect on how we communicate\, what we know\, and what it truly mean
 s to connect. \n\n**Performances:**  April 24\, 2026 7:00 pm  April 2
 5\, 2026 7:00 pm  April 26\, 2026 2:00 pm  May 1\, 2026 7:00 pm  
 May 2\, 2026 7:00 pm  May 3\, 2026 2:00 pm \n\n**Location:**  Napa 
 Valley College Performing Arts Center\, Main Theater  2277 Napa Vallejo H
 wy  Napa\, CA 94558 \n\n**Tickets & Information:**  https://performinga
 rtsnapavalley.org/love-information/
LOCATION:Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center\, Main Theater
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/love-information/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
