BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Experiment Farm Open House and Plant Sale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
UID:2604128JPVgjE0J0eWZOlAS9yyXQ
DESCRIPTION:The Luther Burbank Experiment Farm welcomes you to stop and ex
 plore our historic farm and cottage during Farm Trail's Spring Tour on Sun
 day\, May 3rd from 10AM to 3PM. Free and family friendly!\n\nLuther Burban
 k (1849-1926) was a pioneering botanist who developed more than 800 variet
 ies of plants\, including the Shasta daisy\, Santa Rosa plum\, freestone p
 each\, and the Burbank russet potato - used in 70% of the US's processed p
 otato dishes like french fries.\n\nVisit his experimental farm in Sebastop
 ol\, where he did most of his work\, and see his plants come to life! Volu
 nteers maintain this 3 acre plot\, complete with orchard\, demonstration g
 arden\, and plant nursery where we still grow plants for sale. His cottage
  is beautifully preserved and will be open to the public for this rare occ
 asion.\n\nThere will be heirloom fruit trees and perennial plants for sale
 \, including many of Burbank's finest. Kids activities and a craft sale wi
 th local artists on feature. See the farm at the height of bloom - the Sha
 sta daisies and more will be in full show! Enjoy a picnic at our tables\, 
 explore the self-guided tour\, and find fun local gifts at the Luther Burb
 ank Experiment Farm!
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Experiment Farm
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/25790681533942602/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
