BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T170000
UID:260218_9YTBDBgQkKfeXW1nSb2kg
DESCRIPTION:Lisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter Concert Sunday\, May 3\, 2026 
  3 -5pm\n\nSt. Columba’s Inverness Music Series presents Lisa Lynne & Ar
 yeh Frankfurter: Celtic Harps\, Rare Instruments & Wondrous Stories. \n\n
 Step into an afternoon of enchantment with Lisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter\
 , an internationally acclaimed duo whose music is as expansive as it is in
 timate. Drawing from Celtic\, Nordic\, and Eastern European traditions\, t
 hey weave breathtaking soundscapes on Celtic harps\, Swedish nyckelharpa\,
  Ukrainian bandura\, bouzouki\, cittern\, and other rare instruments. With
  roots in street performing and rock music\, and a combined million-plus a
 lbums sold\, their concerts blend virtuosic musicianship\, original and tr
 aditional melodies\, humor\, and storytelling—inviting audiences into a 
 spellbinding journey of beauty\, wonder\, and joy. \n\nAdvance tickets $2
 5\, $30 at door\n\nLisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter are a multi-instrumental
 ist duo with Celtic Harps\, Swedish Nyckelharpa\, Ukrainian Bandura\, Bouz
 ouki\, Cittern and more. They hail from Oregon and tour extensively\, both
  having successful recording and performing careers built from years of st
 reet performing and a background as rock musicians. They have performed wi
 th some of the biggest names in folk and acoustic music and have sold well
  over a million albums combined. Audiences are spellbound and enchanted wi
 th their unique show of breathtaking music both Traditional and original\,
  with wondrous stories and humor entwined.\n\nGet your tickets at https://
 www.stcolumbasinverness.org/music-series-lisa-aryeh
LOCATION:St. Columba's Inverness
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/lisa-lynne-aryeh-frankf
 urter-concert/18143894/2026-05-03T15
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TJ KLUNE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T153000
UID:260104eD9Vdh0cRU2oED3RoT21ew
DESCRIPTION:SEBASTOPOL --\n\nCopperfield’s Books is delighted to welcome
  perennial staff favorite and New York Times bestselling author TJ Klune 
 to Sebastopol in celebration of his enchanting and deeply stirring new nov
 el — We Burned So Bright.\n\nThis is a ticketed\, off-site event at The
  Sebastopol Community Cultural Center.\n\nEach ticket \\(book\\+tax\\) inc
 ludes admission for one\, seating and a signed hardcover of We Burned So 
 Bright.\n\nJoin us for a reading and warm discussion followed by an audien
 ce Q&A and book-signing with photo opportunities!\n\nScholarships availabl
 e - Dying to attend but can't afford the ticket? Tell us why you can’t m
 iss this special afternoon by emailing jmadsen@copperbook.com\n\nA heart-w
 renching standalone novel by \\#1 New York Times bestselling author TJ K
 lune\,We Burned So Bright follows an elder gay couple on an end-of-the-wo
 rld road-trip.\n\nThe road stretched out before them. No other cars\, just
  the headlights on the blacktop. Above\, the cracked moon in a kaleidoscop
 e sky….\n\nHusbands Don and Rodney have lived a good long life. Together
  they’ve experienced the highest highs of love and family\, and lows so 
 low that they felt like the end of the world.\n\nNow\, the world is ending
  for real. A rogue black hole is coming for Earth and in a month everythin
 g and everyone they’ve ever known will be gone.\n\nSuddenly\, after 40 y
 ears together\, Don and Rodney are out of time. They’re in a race agains
 t the clock to make it from Maine to Washington State to take care of some
  unfinished business before it’s all over.\n\nOn the road they meet thos
 e who refuse to believe death is coming and those who rush to meet it. But
  there are also people living their final days as best they know how—imp
 romptu weddings\, bright burning bonfires\, shared meals\, and new friends
 .\n\nAnd as the black hole draws near\, among ball lightning and under a c
 racked moon in a kaleidoscope sky\, Don and Rodney will look back on their
  lives and ask if their best was good enough.\n\nIs it enough to burn brig
 ht if nothing comes from the ashes?\n\nAuthor: TJ KLUNE \\(he/him\\) is 
 the New York Times and USA Today bestselling\, Lambda Literary Award-w
 inning author of The House in the Cerulean Sea\, Under the Whispering Do
 or\, In the Lives of Puppets\, the Green Creek Series for adults\, the Ex
 traordinaries Series for teens\, and more. Being queer himself\, Klune bel
 ieves it's important—now more than ever—to have accurate\, positive qu
 eer representation in stories.\n\nPRAISE FOR...\n\nFor Somewhere Beyond t
 he Sea: A \\#1 New York Times\, \\#1 USA Today and \\#1 indie bestseller! 
 "An enchanting sequel about found family." — The New York Times For In
  the Lives of Puppets: A New York Times\, Sunday Times and indie bestse
 ller!\n\n"Thoroughly entertaining and deeply stirring." — Chuck Tingle\
 , Hugo Award finalist and author of Camp Damascus For Under the Whisperin
 g Door: A New York Times\, USA Today and indie bestseller!\n\n“Tender
 ness\, wit\, and skillful worldbuilding elevate this delightful tale. Fans
  of queer fantasy won’t want to miss this.” — Publishers Weekly For
  The House in the Cerulean Sea: A New York Times\, USA Today\, and indi
 e bestseller!\n\n"I loved it. It is like being wrapped up in a big gay bla
 nket. Simply perfect." — V.E. Schwab\, \\#1 New York Times bestselling
  author of The Invisible Life of Addie LaRue For The Bones Beneath My Sk
 in: A New York Times\, USA Today\, and indie bestseller!\n\n"An upliftin
 g and curious novel\, a shining dot on an overlapping Venn diagram of sci-
 fi\, fantasy\, adventure and gay romance." — Aurealis
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/tj-klune/17773858/2026-
 05-03T14
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
