BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jazz Adventures
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T190000
UID:251219j_-DtpdVS0WOoj9yW87kKQ
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to my hometown of Healdsburg… in the heart of Sonoma
  wine country\, a town so special that Condé Nast named it one of the fin
 est cities in the country.\n\nI invite you into our world… where our fri
 endships with winemakers\, chefs\, and musicians will create an unforgetta
 ble Adventure just for you. An intimate group trip\, you’ll start each d
 ay from the boutique Hotel Healdsburg in the center of our charming town a
 nd every moment is personally curated by us. We’ll take you to the world
 -renowned regions of Russian River Valley\, Alexander Valley and Sonoma Va
 lley. Along the way\, you’ll enjoy private winery visits to the uber-lux
 ury Robert Young Winery\, the site of one of our very first dates\, and a 
 winery that Eric used to manage\, the legendary Buena Vista Winery. We’l
 l visit the most sought after cult brewery in the world\, the Russian Rive
 r Brewing Co \\(yes\, this is beer in Sonoma as well… trust us … we kn
 ow our alcohol\\).\n\nOh\, you will eat… and eat very well at my favorit
 e Sonoma restaurants including dinner at The Dry Creek Kitchen\, and a pri
 vate lunch that may include more lobster than you’ve ever seen in one pl
 ace\, and of course\, dinner at the most popular restaurant in Healdsburg\
 , The Matheson. You’ll understand why when you visit!\n\nWe love to eat 
 and drink\, but what sets our Adventures apart is the music… a truly exc
 lusive experience you won’t find anywhere else. I will host intimate pri
 vate concerts with my friends and guest musicians\, set in stunning locati
 ons across picturesque Sonoma. Some past artists have included Vincent Ing
 ala\, Richard Elliot\, Peter White and Rick Braun.\n\nAnd\, if you’re in
 terested in extending your stay with me\, there is an optional one-day  ex
 tension add-on that has become the signature day of our domestic Adventure
 s\, where you will experience the very finest Sonoma has to offer.\n\nI ca
 n’t wait to welcome you into this extraordinary place\, a little slice o
 f heaven we call home!\n\nCheers! Mindi 🎶 \\+ Eric 🍷
LOCATION:Hotel Healdsburg
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/106668073?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T170000
UID:260501JjJMfjMFLkypC7RcncpuLw
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th A
 nnual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Galler
 ies\,**continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings togethe
 r over 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed m
 edia.\n\n **The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 
 1st from 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers.** 
 The show highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important ro
 le community arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across gene
 rations.\n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and 
 established artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community
 \, and connection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 
 5:00pm (please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times) and weekends from
  12 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to 
 Donn DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T170000
UID:2605019ODcCIbgGU2kd_vC5aXRzQ
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
