BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T170000
UID:260501TPlRbVKP8k6i5mR9LmB46A
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T170000
UID:260501N5MOwdnC3UaFDOIwYPpiWA
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th A
 nnual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Galler
 ies\,**continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings togethe
 r over 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed m
 edia.\n\n **The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 
 1st from 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers.** 
 The show highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important ro
 le community arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across gene
 rations.\n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and 
 established artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community
 \, and connection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 
 5:00pm (please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times) and weekends from
  12 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to 
 Donn DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
