BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T170000
UID:260501gO3_6tyXG0qD6DoYLfflug
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th A
 nnual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Galler
 ies\,**continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings togethe
 r over 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed m
 edia.\n\n **The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 
 1st from 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers.** 
 The show highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important ro
 le community arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across gene
 rations.\n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and 
 established artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community
 \, and connection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 
 5:00pm (please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times) and weekends from
  12 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to 
 Donn DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T170000
UID:260501V9EyhPwfpUCNZkRxsr9eWg
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Album Tour: Back pOrchEstra at Jack London Lodge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T200000
UID:260430GYcypQf6K0qDsCKy0CQu5g
DESCRIPTION:New American Roots Album Awareness Tour continues! Back pOrchE
 stra at Jack London Lodge and Saloon Concert Series\, Glen Ellen\, Thu May
  7\, 6-8 pm\n\nCelebrating the new album\, "Stories In The Heart\," on Glo
 be Records ...out now and made \\#1 first week of March on 4 charts at Roo
 ts Music Report. Lucky to have such talented players... Candy Girard \\(pl
 ayed w/ Delaney Bramlet\, Tanya Tucker\, Jerry Garcia\\) on violin\, Tim E
 schliman \\(Etta James\, Commander Cody & His Western Airmen\, The Christm
 as Jug Band\\) on vocals & resonator guitar\, Lou Rodriguez \\(Gator Beat\
 \) on drums\, Jen Rund \\(Lumination\, The Real Sarahs\\) on bass\, Gary P
 otterton \\(NRPS\, Texas Chainsaw\\) on guitar.\n\nAlbum is available ever
 ywhere ...streaming / downloads at: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\nLPs and CDs
  at https://www.globerecords.com and everywhere\n\nFacebook event page: ht
 tps://www.facebook.com/events/1642368653696179\n\n13740 Arnold Drive Glen 
 Ellen\, CA 95442 - \\(707\\) 938-8510\n\nA broad range of Indie Rock and A
 mericana and the American Roots styles that inspired it: country blues\, Z
 ydeco\, roots rock\, Tex Mex\, rockabilly\, Singer-Songwriter\, Motown\, B
 razilian and Louisiana music. This combo\, sprung out of the pandemic has 
 developed a unique\, catchy\, funky\, moody sound\, drawing from the varie
 d past. Comparison's have been made to the music of Big Al Anderson \\(NRB
 Q\\)\, The Band\, JJ Cale\, Asleep At The Wheel\, Dan Hicks\, Buddy & Juli
 e Miller\, Jesse Ed Davis & Levon Helm.\n\nJack London Saloon: Experience 
 quintessential Glen Ellen like the locals do. Steeped in turn of the centu
 ry history and charm\, The Jack London Saloon offers a spacious and beauti
 ful Creekside Patio... savor the serene setting beside the Sonoma Creek. E
 xperience a vintage landmark among Sonoma Wine Country restaurants. The Sa
 loon features wine country comfort food and the best burger in Sonoma. The
  beverage list highlights an incredible variety of Wine Country vintages\,
  craft beers\, and cocktails.\n\n"...The guitars slam like saloon doors\, 
 the violin traces lines that oscillate between melancholy and jubilation\,
  the rhythm section moves forward with a tranquil groove that never rushes
  but never falters... Back pOrchEstra delivers a luminous\, earthy\, profo
 undly human record. An album that makes you want to sit on a porch\, watch
  the sunset\, and let the stories do their work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zic
 azine \\(translated from French\\) https://www.zicazic.com/zicazine/index.
 php?option=content&task=view&id=18836\n\n"...What sets 'Stories In The Hea
 rt' apart is its sense of balance. Resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drum
 s\, percussion\, dobro\, and Telecaster create a flexible\, roots-forward 
 palette that allows Back Porchestra to move between styles fluidly. The so
 ngs echo traditions without reenacting them\, keeping one foot in the past
  and the other firmly planted in the present." - Vince's Hot Picks \\(Best
  of 2026\\) New Releases Now\n\nsee our music video\, "Dusty Road I'm On" 
 video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number with a C
 ajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\nOur "Voices In
  My Head \\(Genre Whiplash\\)" made the Top 100 Albums at Alt.Country Spec
 ialty Chart.\n\nChoose your music service: https://orcd.co/dw640r4\n\nLPs\
 , CDs\, and USB-Music Cards available all over\, including https://www.glo
 berecords.com\n\n"It's one fine album" - Ben Fong-Torres \\(Rolling Stone\
 , Almost Famous\\)\n\n"...evokes artists from multiple decades over the la
 st century and embraces everything from indie-rock and Americana to Celtic
 \, Motown\, and Western swing. If you need a reference point\, look to ban
 ds like Dan Hicks and His Hot Licks and Asleep at the Wheel\, whose record
 s also draw on disparate sources." - Jeff Burger\, Americana Highway\n\nse
 e!:\n\nhttp://www.BackPorchEstra.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/p
 laylist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nhttps://www.facebook.co
 m/BackPorchEstra\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\nSpotify: 
 https://open.spotify.com/artist/0s4VMCtb1EMddafnDPZDDM?si=cGVFpp1JROaDEvSr
 JpKVjA\n\nrootsrock \\#americanrootsmusic \\#americanamusic \\#rockabillym
 usic \\#twangyguitar \\#backporchestra \\#acousticmusic
LOCATION:Jack London Lodge
URL:http://www.BackPorchEstra.com#cal
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa 4-Week Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T203000
UID:260426YQF6Y3fLlEuMKa7wiW6quw
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nMay 7- May 28\n\nThis is a beginner cuban salsa—you will l
 earn your basic footwork and turns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn the 
 fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, including body movement\, rhythm\, musicalit
 y\, footwork\, partner connection\, and partnerwork patterns inspired by a
 uthentic Cuban dance culture.\n\nWe focus on proper technique\, coordinati
 on\, flow\, and natural body expression\, while also building confidence a
 nd strong foundations.\n\nClasses are structured with:\n\n• Warm-up and 
 body movement\n\n• Footwork and rhythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork tech
 nique\n\n• Short combinations and practical applications\n\nOur goal is 
 to help you understand how to dance salsa\, not just memorize steps — de
 veloping timing\, connection\, and a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing.\
 n\nCome dance with us\, grow your technique\, and experience the energy an
 d flavor of Cuba in a supportive and welcoming environment.\n\nBook your s
 pot\n\nDate & Time: 4week class\, May 7- May 28\n\nThursdays @ 7:30 PM\n\n
 Address: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minu
 tes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
