SUMMARY:Blockprint Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T183000
UID:2604035TImPb6ZKka5RNSJUhPlbw
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in the beautiful Marietta Tasting room for a sp
 ecial hands-on block printing workshop.  Naomi will guide attendees throu
 gh the timeless craft of block printing—an ancient relief technique wher
 e hand-carved designs are inked and pressed to create one-of-a-kind prints
  on fabric or paper.\n\nSpend a creative evening designing and printing be
 spoke pieces—perhaps a set of napkins\, a table runner\, or a festive te
 a towel—to bring art and intention to your table. Enjoy slowing down\, c
 onnecting\, and leaning into your creative process\, and take home your ha
 ndmade creation as a keepsake. We will have items available for printing\,
  or you can bring something from home you would like to adorn or create a 
 pattern on. Come with a design idea and leave with your own rubber stamp 
 to create with after the class.\n\nLight snacks and the first pour of wine
  are included.
LOCATION:Marietta Cellar's Tasting Room 
URL:https://www.fielddayca.com/event-details/blockprint-workshop-at-mariet
 ta-cellars-2026-04-02-16-00
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAST COAST SWING with Mark Novak (4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T203000
UID:260401ks2XAHyaA0CMnwuJ3Go9jA
DESCRIPTION:East Coast Swing: 4 week class\n\nMay 7 – May 28\n\nThursday
  7:30 PM – 8:30 PM\n\nGet ready to jump\, jive\, and swing! Join us for 
 an energetic and fun introduction to the classic East Coast Swing. This p
 artner dance is a popular\, lively style derived from Lindy Hop\, danced t
 o big band\, jazz\, rock and roll\, and blues music.\n\nWhat to Expect\n\n
 Our comprehensive class is designed for All Levels!\n\nYou’ll learn the
  fundamental six-count basic step\, essential leading and following techni
 ques\, and foundational moves like the change of place and simple turns. W
 e’ll ensure you have a solid foundation to hit the dance floor right awa
 y!\n\nKey Details\n\n• Level: All Levels Welcome!\n\n• Duration: 4 w
 eeks\n\n• No Partner Necessary: We rotate partners frequently in class 
 to ensure everyone gets to dance and learn the lead and follow roles effec
 tively. Feel free to bring a partner\, but it’s certainly not required!\
 n\n• What to Wear: Comfortable clothes that allow for movement\, and sm
 ooth-soled shoes \\(avoid sticky rubber soles\\).\n\nCome discover the joy
  of East Coast Swing! It’s a fantastic workout and a great way to meet n
 ew people.\n\nAbout Mark\n\nMark Novak has a professional dance career wh
 ich spans nearly 40 years. He has taught as a star teacher for studios and
  ballrooms throughout the Bay Area and Central Calif. He was the former Di
 rector of Bay West Ballroom of both San Rafael and Fresno. He has danced a
 ll over North America as both a competitor and floor show dancer\, feature
 d on stage\, film\, television and industry events. In 2005 he won the Ris
 ing Star Latin Dance Champion of Hawaii title and Rising Star Ballroom tit
 le of Colorado.\n\nHe was the Latin Representative for the Western States 
 in the team match event of the Dancesport Superbowl Series 2002 at the pre
 stigious Ohio Star Ball. He is a master teacher\, recognized by the Imperi
 al Society of Teachers of Dance and the National Dance Council of America.
  He looks forward to working with the Salsa Dance Academy of Marin.\n\nDat
 e & Time:  Thursday 7:30 PM – 8:30 PM \\(4 weeks\\)\, May 7 – May 28\
 n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 m
 inutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/east-coast-swing-with-m
 ark-novak-4/18489684/2026-05-07T19
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
