BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mother's Day Magic at NVMY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T160000
UID:260501pSRUT68bgUKYSyR8ZFwhVQ
DESCRIPTION:It’s time to celebrate the women who act as our real-life Fa
 iry Godmothers—the ones who transform the everyday into something truly 
 magical.\n\nGive her the royal treatment and prepare her for the "ball" wi
 th a day of art. No transformation is complete without the right accessori
 es!\n\nThis Mother's Day weekend\, spend $50 or more in the Napa Valley M
 useum Yountville store and you’ll be gifted a collectible Mary Blair-in
 spired NVMY pin.\n\nDon’t wait for the clock to strike midnight!
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/mothers-day-magic-at-nvmy
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mother's Day at the MAC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T170000
UID:260501nJ-pb5ZrXEuIy88J2DnKXw
DESCRIPTION:Our beloved Big Butter Bench has officially moved indoors to
  the lobby. This is the perfect spot for a commemorative Mother’s Day ph
 oto.\n\nAfter your photo op\, explore our curated Butter Collection in t
 he Museum Store. From sleek home goods to thoughtful keepsakes\, we have t
 he perfect gift for moms and the important women in our lives who apprecia
 te "smooth" style.\n\nSpend $25 or more at The MAC store and receive a c
 omplementary MAC Butter Pin as our gift to you!
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum of Art and Culture (The MAC)
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/mothers-day-at-the-mac
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T170000
UID:260501VpF-pN5zGEayuGsfbt7xPQ
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Lives 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T210000
UID:260501TPwCsr81wU2h3mw6W461tg
DESCRIPTION:The Healdsburg Museum will host **History Lives**\n\n**2026**\
 , its signature annual gala fundraiser\, on **Friday\, May 8\, from 6:00 t
 o 9:00 p.m.** at\n\n**Appellation Healdsburg**\, acclaimed restaurateur Ch
 arlie Palmer’s new north-Healdsburg\n\ndestination. The evening celebrat
 es the Museum’s 50th anniversary and honors longtime\n\ncommunity leader
 s **Mike McGuire** and **Erika McGuire** as this year’s Pioneer Award ho
 norees.\n\nTickets are $250 per person and are on sale now at\n\nhttps://s
 ecure.qgiv.com/event/historylives2026/.
LOCATION:Appellation Healdsburg
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/event/historylives2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T170000
UID:260501Pk91eAKi70O9f-RvlhrC9A
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th A
 nnual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Galler
 ies\,**continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings togethe
 r over 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed m
 edia.\n\n **The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 
 1st from 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers.** 
 The show highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important ro
 le community arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across gene
 rations.\n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and 
 established artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community
 \, and connection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 
 5:00pm (please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times) and weekends from
  12 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to 
 Donn DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
