DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T130000
UID:260429oeiustkrFUuywjKaEbTftA
DESCRIPTION:Get Special "VIT" Access to Bay Area Nature\n\nThe Solano Land
  Trust is currently working with partners in hopes of opening a new sectio
 n of the Ridge Trail across the Vallejo Swett Ranch Property that will con
 nect the Blue Rock Springs Park and Hiddenbrooke Ridge Trail sections.   
 With the completion of the Vallejo Swett trail section\, the Ridge Trail i
 n Solano County will extend from the Benicia-Martinez Bridge \\(Carquinesz
  Strait Scenic Loop Trail\\) to the Napa County line adjacent to Lynch Can
 yon Open Space Park. This connection will provide new opportunities for ou
 tdoor recreation for the residents of western Solano County.\n\nThe total
  distance for this out-and-back hike will be about 5 miles\, starting at t
 he Blue Rock Springs Trailhead.\n\nTerrain Types: cross country hiking\, r
 anch roads\, paved roads.\n\nParking Fee: $6 Vallejo Residents\, $8 non-re
 sidents
LOCATION:Blue Rock Springs Park
URL:https://support.ridgetrail.org/event/2026-vallejo-swett-vit/e778859
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
