BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: The Poetic Landscape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T180000
UID:260318AmYTjvwc0UK2oKZ39B0Uog
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  3/13/26\n\n**APRIL EXHIBIT: THE 
 POETIC LANDSCAPE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  March 30  – April 26\, 2026\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, APRIL 4\, 2026\, 3-5 pm: Join us to meet KAREN MILL
 ER and PHYLLIS RAPP\;  celebrate the show and enjoy a poetry reading by f
 eatured guest\, Linda Loveland Reid\, gallery artist and published author.
   Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthly drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Karen Miller\,** presents **The Poetic Landscape\,** pa
 stel paintings that convey Miller’s personal experience in connecting wi
 th the intrinsic beauty of natural places. In these pieces\, color\, fluid
  shapes and rhythmic design combine to create an uplifting mood – a true
  poetic interlude.  Evoking a happy mood\, “Geyserville Sunflowers\,”
  turning to the sun by nature\, joyfully dance in its luminescence. By the
  river’s edge\, concentric reflections conjure a calm sense of wellbeing
  in “Fetch.”  The viewer feels welcomed by a warm embrace entering a 
 shaded secret spot in “September Trellis.”  Focused on local scenes\,
  these works truly hone in on the stunning landscape out our doors.  Mill
 er remarked “ As I contemplate the very real places of beauty surroundin
 g us\, I try to express my painterly response in hopes it will engender re
 cognition by the viewers.” \n\nMeet the artist: Miller will be hosting 
 the Gallery on March 30\, April 5 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n The Stai
 rway Smallworks Showcase features **Phyllis Rapp’s Magic Moments\,** a c
 ollection of watercolors that create an atmosphere that is both introspect
 ive and magical.  Familiar domestic scenes are transformed as humans inte
 ract with animals and birds in floral settings.  In “Silent Watcher” 
 the red-headed young woman’s green eyes lock onto ours as she stares ahe
 ad\, flanked by her avian companion.  Experiencing these works is a like 
 taking a mini-step on the wild side\, an exciting and fun experience.\n\nM
 eet the artist: Rapp will be hosting the Gallery on March 30 and April 10 
 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\
 , April 2\, 5 – 6 pm.  The theme for the 2026 kickoff event is Bouquets
  to Art.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is
  a community event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries p
 articipating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Cente
 r Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 
 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Con
 tact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:French Garden Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T160000
UID:260228YCu59bpVS02qWCdnDPyqXQ
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 9\, 2026\n\n12-4 p.m.  |  21 & Older Only\n\n
 $45 per person\n\nHeld just in time for Mother’s Day weekend\, Dry Creek
  Vineyard’s French Garden Market invites guests to step into the charm o
 f the French countryside with a festive outdoor celebration in the heart o
 f Dry Creek Valley. Visitors can browse a thoughtfully curated collection 
 of local artisans offering handcrafted treasures — from chic clothing an
 d jewelry to gourmet foods and home goods — perfect for spring gifting.\
 n\nGuests are invited to sip and savor the release of the winery’s newes
 t vintages of Petite Zin Rosé and Sauvignon Blanc while enjoying live mus
 ic by electric violinist Maya Victoria\, who brings a lively twist to mode
 rn pop favorites. The event also features Claudine\, the winery’s vintag
 e Citroën mobile bar and centerpiece of the wine garden\, along with deli
 cious bites from a local food pop-up. Attendees are encouraged to relax\, 
 linger\, and make a day of it.
LOCATION:Dry Creek Vineyard
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/french-garden-market/18
 234413/2026-05-09T12
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T000000
UID:260227y0AzIQ_G00GKSsfZ1kaebw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Tasting Notes
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107935486?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poor Man's Whiskey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T000000
UID:260224JoaUCT_KIEaldxIBNjeERg
DESCRIPTION:"In the end\, they are an original distillation\, a tasty burn
  that goes down with a kick and lingers beautifully when it hits your gut.
 "- Dennis Cook\, Jambase.com  Poor Man's Whiskey plays "High Octane Hooten
 anny" music…Dance\, laugh\, sing.   Emerging from the San Francisco bay 
 area music scene this quintet has developed a sound that is eclectic and e
 ngaging.  PMW has been winning over national audiences with their upbeat p
 erformances\, zany stage antics\, and infectious songs.   While seamlessly
  integrating acoustic and electric instruments the band weaves tales of ev
 eryday life\, inviting the audience to become a part of each show.     PMW
  has released three studio albums\, "Train to California" \\(2003\\)\, "Ro
 adside Attraction"\\(2005\\)\, and in 2009: "Dark Side of the Moonshine" \
 \(a double disk set featuring original music as well as the bluegrass inte
 rpretation of the Pink Floyd classic album\\).    Notable festivals and sh
 ows:  Hardly Strictly Bluegrass Festival\, High Sierra Music Festival\, Ka
 te Wolf Music Festival\,  The Fillmore\, SF\; Harmony Festival\; Strawberr
 y Music Festival\; The Great American Music Hall\;  The Summer Melt Down\,
  Las Tortugas\; finals of the Telluride Bluegrass Festival. For PMW calend
 ar please visit www.PoorMansWhiskey.com
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107805721?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
