BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirit Guides
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
UID:260313nExbEmxWk0inum2I19XFWg
DESCRIPTION:Spirit Guides: Fantastical Creatures from the Workshop of Jaco
 bo and María Ángeles features brightly colored\, richly patterned sculp
 tures depicting imaginary hybrid animals that serve as spirit guides and a
 strological embodiments of human character. Inspired by the Zapotec calend
 ar\, the exhibition includes eight large-scale works organized by Denver B
 otanic Gardens.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
UID:260430EnESoUYZ80SOFuOt7ErZjw
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirit Guides Guided Walking Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T113000
UID:260427KmpYXv_Lq0CCOXhJzyTuww
DESCRIPTION:Join knowledgeable volunteer Garden Guides for special tours o
 f Spirit Guides at Sonoma Botanical Garden on select Saturdays during the 
 run of the exhibition. Experience the updated entrance to our California O
 aks Trail and discover the vibrant\, monumental sculptures by Jacobo and M
 aría Ángeles\, hearing stories about the works’ cultural inspirations\
 , symbolic meanings\, and connections with the natural world. Our voluntee
 rs will enrich your visit with insights into the artists’ process\, the 
 Zapotec influences behind the spirit animals\, and how the exhibition comp
 lements the surrounding landscape. These engaging English language tours o
 ffer context and conversation that deepen your appreciation of both the ar
 t and the Garden.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makers Market™ Local Artist Fair @ First Street Napa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
UID:260420fWrjqzGerkGEvNu2LXAvjw
DESCRIPTION:Join Makers Market™ to kick off the 2026 Local Artist Fairs 
 at First Street Napa! Get ready for another season of creativity\, communi
 ty\, and incredible goods made here in the Bay Area. Come support talented
  makers\, discover beautiful artisan products\, and enjoy a fun-filled day
  outdoors!\n\nWHEN? Saturday\, May 9 | 11am - 5pm\n\nWHERE? First Street N
 apa in Napa\, CA\n\n- 40\\+ local makers\n\n- Handmade jewelry\, pottery\,
  fragrances\, candles\, bath and body\, apparel\, leather goods\, and more
 !\n\n- Kid- and pet-friendly\n\n- Enjoy live music by local musicians\n\n-
  Stop into the Makers Market™ brick-and-mortar store \\(in Suite 301\, a
 djacent to the fair\\) and shop even more unique\, American-made products.
 \n\nShare with your shopping buddies and mark your calendars! Can't wait t
 o see you there!\n\n- - -\n\nAre you a maker looking to sell your products
  at the Local Artist Street Fair? Register here:\n\nhttps://makersmarket.u
 s/maker-registration/\n\n- - -\n\nMakers Market is locally founded and ind
 ependently owned\, with brick-and-mortar stores in Alpharetta\, Napa\, San
 tana Row\, Lafayette\, and Mill Valley. We aim to bring you products that 
 honor the ideals of American craftsmanship and are modern\, handmade\, and
  sustainably produced. Join us in our mission of Rebuilding the Legacy of 
 American Made\, while supporting our local artists\, local economies\, and
  the community. Come visit one of our stores today!\n\nhttps://makersmarke
 t.us/locations/
LOCATION:First Street Napa
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1770863670938322/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Morning Hike and Tasting at the Ridge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
UID:260420IamX2UU6WUun7qP39xM5nw
DESCRIPTION:As featured in San Francisco Chronicle list of “10 wine tast
 ings in Napa and Sonoma with ‘wellness’ activities like hiking\, bikin
 g and yoga”\n\nEmbark on a guided “grape-to-glass” journey that begi
 ns with artisan trail treats before ascending into our dramatically terrac
 ed hillside vineyards.\n\nAs you navigate the estate\, your host will prov
 ide deep insights into our diverse ecosystems and the geological significa
 nce of our Stags Leap District location. You will explore why these distin
 ct sites produce such storied wines while enjoying a comparative tasting t
 hat showcases the nuance and variation across our premier appellations.\n\
 nPricing: $100 per guest | $80 per club member\n\nAvailability: Groups of 
 1–12 guests\n\nPace: Moderate hike with challenging inclines\; weather p
 ermitting\n\nAttire: Strictly no open-toed shoes. Appropriate hiking footw
 ear is require
LOCATION:Pine Ridge Vineyards
URL:https://www.pineridgevineyards.com/events/morning-hike-and-tasting-at-
 the-ridge/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Beginner Hiking for Fitness Spring 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T120000
UID:260413bC3NkGvd1EqUs6EeGsvy3Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe series costs $80 (plus a $10 parking fee per visi
 t. Note that the Sugarloaf Annual Pass is $59 and valid at Sug
 arloaf and Jack London SHP)\, or free-of-cost for participants wi
 th a March 2026 or newer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medical
  Provider. Click https://sugarloafpark.org/activities/parks-rx-program/
  for information on our Park Rx program and to download the fo
 rm. The number of **available Park Rx tickets is limited**\; **pl
 ease have your Rx ready at the time of sign up**.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffspring26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
