BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild Women Gathering at Mandala Springs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T150000
UID:260130BFtzIvL-pU2YCHHBo31ZAA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for The Wild Women Gathering\, a chance to experience 
 the Wild Women Rising magic firsthand during this free weekend retreat in 
 wild Cobb\, Northern California \\(room \\+ board only\\). Settle into Man
 dala Springs and let yourself be cared for: soak in the hot tub\, enjoy lo
 ve-catered meals\, move with yoga\, and treat yourself to massage. Spend t
 ime in nature. Spend time with yourself. Rest. And then… the shifts. Wit
 ness something rare and powerful: a room of strangers becoming vulnerable\
 , intimate\, and safe. With guidance and support\, you'll feel seen\, held
 \, and loved\, and from that place\, deep re-patterning becomes possible. 
 You'll leave with: ✨ Awakened intuition and confidence to know your path
 \, and the courage to follow it ✨ A proven approach to move through fear
  so you can share your gifts ✨ Your wild woman warrior ignited-calling i
 n creativity\, sensuality\, and purpose
LOCATION:Mandala Springs
URL:https://www.mandala.org/upcoming-events/2026/5/14/wild-women-gathering
 -at-mandala-springs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pond Farm Artist in Residence 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T000000
UID:260424VCJZtbUiAEuRWmNL41J04Q
DESCRIPTION:Pond Farm Pottery is the former home and studio of renowned ma
 ster potter\, artist\, and educator\, Marguerite Wildenhain\, and a new Na
 tional Historic Landmark. Pond Farm is located above Armstrong Redwoods\, 
 in beautiful Guerneville\, California. Spend your time in a private cabin 
 at Pond Farm Pottery. Breathtaking inspirational views. Miles and miles of
  hiking. 5 minute drive to Armstrong Redwoods\; 15 minute drive to downtow
 n Guerneville for shopping/art/restaurants/wine tasting\; 30 minutes to th
 e Sonoma Coast\; and approximately 1 hr 45 minutes to San Francisco. Pond 
 Farm Pottery offers an Artist-in-Residence \\(AiR\\) program funded by  Ar
 ts in California Parks \, a program of CA State Parks\, Parks California\,
  and California Arts Council.  Click here for more information about AiR a
 t Pond Farm . Visit Pond Farm by registering for a docent-led tour on our 
  events page  Fill out the application here
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/pond-farm-artist-in-residence-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
