BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Immigration Update 2026 | Meeting the moment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T130000
UID:260502TeIBpkuLYkKe32lgJ2cEww
DESCRIPTION:Immigration Update 2026\n\nMeeting the moment with truth\, res
 ilience and courage\n\nLos Cien Sonoma County will once again convene comm
 unity leaders\, advocates\, service providers\, and residents for a timely
  and important conversation on immigration and its impact on our region.\n
 \nAt a time marked by deep uncertainty\, fear\, and rapid change\, this pr
 ogram will create space to better understand the current realities facing 
 immigrant communities in Sonoma County\, honor the resilience and courage 
 of those most affected\, and highlight the local organizations and leaders
  responding with care\, action\, and commitment. Featuring keynote remarks
  from Professor Bill Ong Hing\, the program will offer insight into the br
 oader immigration landscape while grounding the conversation in local chal
 lenges\, community response\, and the work still ahead.\n\nKeynote Speaker
 \n\nProfessor Bill Ong Hing\, University of San Francisco\n\nAssociate Dea
 n for Faculty Scholarship\, Professor\, Founding Director of the Immigrati
 on and Deportation Defense Clinic\, and Dean's Circle Scholar\n\nPanel Spe
 akers\n\nNicole A. Gorney\, Vital Immigrant Defense Advocacy and Services 
 \\(VIDAS\\)\n\nSupervising Attorney\, Removal Defense &amp\; Farmworker Pr
 ograms\n\nVicki Handron\, Sonoma Immigrant Services\n\nExecutive Director\
 n\nYeni Rodriguez\, Child Parent Institute\n\nCommunity Health Worker Prog
 ram Manager\n\nMore Panel Speakers coming soon&hellip\;\n\nJoin us as we m
 eet this moment with truth\, resilience\, and courage&mdash\;and explore h
 ow we can stay informed\, connected\, and united in building hope\, healin
 g\, and access for every generation.
LOCATION:The Backdrop @ Becoming Independent
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/immigration-update-2026?af
 f=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
