BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers Meeting Small But Mighty: Crafting a Winning Eleva
 tor Pitch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T133000
UID:260428e22QKPg3REiSVwM2ZEEPLw
DESCRIPTION:Redwood Writers General Meeting - Lisa Manterfield: Small But 
 Mighty: Crafting a Winning Elevator Pitch\n\nWhen and Where:\n\nMay 16\, 2
 026\, 11 a.m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa\n\nPlease bring something savory
  or sweet to share in our potluck!\n\n“So\, what’s your book about?”
  It’s a simple question that strikes terror in many writers. How do you 
 condense your 300-page masterpiece into a few sentences without making you
 r audience’s eyes glaze over? In this class\, you’ll learn the key ele
 ments that will draw the reader in and make your story feel both unique an
 d universal. Plus\, you’ll see how this short piece of sales copy forms 
 the foundation of your query letter\, book jacket copy\, and more. Come wi
 th your latest book premise and leave with a winning pitch.\n\nAbout the P
 resenter: Lisa Manterfield is the award-winning author of five novels and 
 two works of non-fiction\, including All Our Lies Are True\, a psychologi
 cal suspense that Publishers Weekly calls “gut-wrenching…and legitimat
 ely gripping.” As a book coach and editor\, she loves to help writers ta
 ke their work to the next level and is a regular instructor for Stanford C
 ontinuing Studies Creative Writing program. Originally from northern Engla
 nd\, she now lives in Northern California with her husband and cat. When n
 ot writing\, she can be found hiking in the redwoods and digging in her ve
 getable garden. Her new mystery novel\, Invisible Ink\, will be published
  by Thomas & Mercer in 2027.\n\nLearn more at LisaManterfield.com\, or sa
 y hello on Instagram or Facebook
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/may-2026-lisa-manterfield/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
