BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sourdough from Scratch with Monica Flaherty at Gold Ridge Organic 
 Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T130000
UID:2604274pp9Pyz_HUWyH5v_3swcNQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a 3-hour hands-on sourdough making class at Gold R
 idge Organic Farms\, led by Monica Flaherty of the Sebastopol Sourdough Co
 mpany. Spend three immersive hours in our charming Apple Cottage learning 
 the art and science of sourdough bread making.\n\nMonica will walk you thr
 ough everything you need to know — how wild yeast and fermentation work\
 , why sourdough differs from commercial yeast bread\, and how to read your
  dough. You'll also cover starter care and feeding\, mixing and hydration 
 ratios\, shaping and scoring techniques\, and the secrets to achieving tha
 t perfect crust and open crumb.\n\nEvery guest will leave with an active s
 tarter\, a feeding schedule and care guide\, a shaped dough in a banneton 
 ready to bake at home\, and their very own apron to take home as a keepsak
 e. The experience also includes a ride across the farm on our beloved appl
 e-themed trolley to the Apple Cottage.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/606241/sour
 dough-from-scratch-with-monica-flaherty
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Room in the Castle - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T190000
UID:260426ODUp_TVFm0GKd6kdZbohyw
DESCRIPTION:A Room in the Castle is a feminist reimagining of William Shak
 espeare’s Hamlet\, written by prolific American playwright Lauren M. Gu
 nderson. The play shifts the perspective of the classic tragedy to focus e
 ntirely on the women of Elsinore: Ophelia\, Queen Gertrude\, and Ophelia
 ’s handmaid\, Anna.\n\nThe troubled\, grieving Prince of Denmark is neve
 r far from the thoughts of Ophelia\, a caretaker to Ophelia\, and the Quee
 n of Denmark. Playwright Lauren Gunderson does a masterful job re-imaginin
 g the women trapped by class\, circumstances\, expectations\, and desire w
 ithin the castle’s walls. Each\, in their own way\, follows the queen’
 s edict for women—to “obey\, agree\, assist”—until they absolutely
  do not. This play dances and duels with Hamlet\, foregrounding the women 
 in the play and re-imagining them with agency\, vitality\, and radical hea
 rts eager for a more hopeful ending.\n\nThe women of Hamlet have moments t
 hat are wholly their own. They own the stage—and our hearts.  ­— DC 
 TheaterArts\n\nFeaturing: Tatiana – Luisa Sermol / Ophelia – Marie Sad
 d / Gertrude – Leontyne Mbele Mbong\n\nDirected by Amy Kossow: "I have s
 een Hamlet so many times but here finally is a chance to stop and ask what
  the women are doing while all the men plot and scheme.  Lauren Gunderson
  gives Gertrude and Ophelia \\(along with a mysterious third woman\\) a wh
 ole play all to themselves\, and as the events of Hamlet unfold around the
 m\, these three create their own brilliant stories.\n\n- Sponsored in part
  by Melinda & Paul Pressler -\n\n-Theatre - Programmed by Aldo Billingslea
  and Amy Kossow -
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://the222.org/product/a-room-in-the-castle/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:18th Annual Kite Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T140000
UID:260425qfV9CBqJ3UeWrPtsuK-4Qg
DESCRIPTION:The Annual Lynch Canyon Kite Festival is a free event open to 
 everyone! Lynch Canyon is an open space park owned by Solano Land Trust an
 d operated through partnership by Solano County Parks. Lynch Canyon has tr
 ails for hiking\, biking and equestrian use among the windswept rolling hi
 lls between Fairfield and Vallejo\, making it the perfect place to fly a k
 ite.\n\nWhat to be prepared for:\n\nAll ages and ability levels are welcom
 e!\n\nDogs are not allowed \\(to protect wildlife\, rare plants\, and free
 -range cattle\\).\n\nExpect rough\, uneven ground.\n\nWe do our best to mi
 nimize it for the festival\, but expect some cow manure as this is a worki
 ng ranch where free-range cattle roam as they please.\n\nThere is no drink
 ing water.\n\nTake only pictures\, leave only footprints.\n\nMaintain a sa
 fe distance from cattle and wildlife\, and be aware that this is tick\, mo
 untain lion\, and potentially rattlesnake country.\n\nWhat to bring:\n\nA 
 kite.\n\nDrinking water.\n\nA picnic lunch.\n\nProtection from sun\, wind\
 , fog and rain.\n\nBoots or sturdy closed-toe shoes.\n\nYour friends and f
 amily!
LOCATION:Lynch Canyon Open Space Park
URL:https://solanolandtrust.org/events-news/recurring-events/kite-festival
 .html
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
