DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T170000
UID:260313dD5Sqe-0hkG8uBXTXdILCg
DESCRIPTION:Spirit Guides: Fantastical Creatures from the Workshop of Jaco
 bo and María Ángeles features brightly colored\, richly patterned sculp
 tures depicting imaginary hybrid animals that serve as spirit guides and a
 strological embodiments of human character. Inspired by the Zapotec calend
 ar\, the exhibition includes eight large-scale works organized by Denver B
 otanic Gardens.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T200000
UID:260502LQdG9jmubUK5BlxRpKgH6Q
DESCRIPTION:Joyce Grant Vallejo local singer\, Joyce Grant returns to the 
 Ferry Taproom with her powerful mix of jazz\, blues\, and R&B. Joyce Grant
  singer/songwriter\, determined at an early age that she was going to be a
  singer and spent her elementary and high school days performing in choir 
 and musical theater. She is the great-great-niece of famed ragtime compose
 r Scott Joplin and has written lyrics to four of his songs. She has partic
 ipated in the West Coast Ragtime Festival for several years. City Swing st
 arted a new chapter in 2007 with jazz singer Joyce Grant. She is the lead 
 vocalist for City Swing\, an 18 piece big band. Grant has been singing jaz
 z in Bay Area venues for over 20 years. A mezzo-soprano with a voice like 
 dark honey\, Grant has a performance resume which includes a wide range of
  venues including the Empire Plush Room and Zingari Ristaurante in San Fra
 ncisco\, the Ledson Hotel in Sonoma\, Sam's Chowder House & Cetrella in Ha
 lf Moon Bay\, the Sticky Rice in Fairfield\, Carneros in Napa\, Slates in 
 Walnut Creek\, Joe's of Lafayette\, and the Woodminster Amphitheater just 
 to name a few. Born in Texarkana\, the town where Scott Joplin was raised\
 , Grant moved to Oakland as a child where she started singing with the Nor
 th Oakland Baptist Church Youth Choir. Since that time she has earned the 
 respect of singers and musicians alike performing professionally in San Fr
 ancisco\, the East Bay\, Walnut Creek\, Napa Valley and beyond. Her unique
  shows consist of a blend of jazz\, blues\, country western\, Rhythm and B
 lues\, and funk. Her vocal interpretations range from sensitive to powerfu
 l to cheeky over a broad spectrum of charts. Joyce Grant is a member of AS
 CAP.
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-0516202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T170000
UID:260430Olxcg1clR0WSXiRCXxEN4w
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
