BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Tarot: Back to Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
UID:2605020umiAVP7CE-y2am0DfPhng
DESCRIPTION:Return to the heart of tarot in this &ldquo\;Back to Basics&rd
 quo\; Tea &amp\; Tarot class\, designed to help you build a strong\, clear
 \, and confident foundation in your reading practice. This is where intuit
 ion meets structure\, guiding you beyond memorization.\n\nWe'll explore th
 e core elements of tarot\, including card meanings\, symbolism\, and simpl
 e yet powerful spreads. You'll learn how to trust your interpretations\, c
 reate consistency in your readings\, and deepen your connection with your 
 deck.\n\nWhether you're brand new or looking to refresh your skills\, this
  class offers a grounded\, supportive space to reconnect with what matters
  most: clarity\, confidence\, and your intuitive voice.
LOCATION:Songbird Community Healing Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/tea-and-tarot-back-to-basi
 cs-2?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Tarot: Element of Air Alchemy of Thought
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T143000
UID:260430LomxFjitxUOEo5Yu9HKXeA
DESCRIPTION: Air: Mental Alchemy Shadow Work\n\nTea &amp\; Tarot &bull\; T
 he Alchemy of Thought\n\nSunday\, May 17\n\nAir is the realm of the mind &
 mdash\; language\, memory\, belief\, perception\, and meaning. It shapes h
 ow we interpret reality and how reality responds to us. In this Air-themed
  Tea &amp\; Tarot gathering\, we enter the subtle territory of mental shad
 ow work: the unconscious thought forms\, internalized voices\, and belief 
 systems that quietly influence our choices\, communication\, and sense of 
 self.\n\nMental shadow is not simply &ldquo\;negative thinking.&rdquo\; It
  includes inherited narratives\, protective strategies of the psyche\, int
 ernalized authority\, and unexamined assumptions that once served a purpos
 e but now restrict growth. Through tarot\, we gently bring these patterns 
 into conscious awareness\, where they can be met with discernment rather t
 han suppression.\n\nThis is not a therapeutic intervention\, nor is it pre
 dictive. It is a sacred inquiry into how the mind constructs meaning &mdas
 h\; and how awareness restores agency.\n\nWhat We'll Explore\n\n    &bull\
 ;    The origins of recurring thought loops and mental habits\n\n    &bull
 \;    Internalized voices from family\, culture\, or past experiences\n\n 
    &bull\;    How fear\, control\, or avoidance shape perception\n\n    &b
 ull\;    Where clarity\, truth\, or expression is being unconsciously rest
 rained\n\n    &bull\;    The difference between intuition\, thought\, and 
 conditioned belief\n\nAir teaches us that thought is creative &mdash\; but
  not all thoughts are true. When we learn to listen beneath the noise of t
 he mind\, we reclaim authorship of our inner world and restore integrity t
 o our voice.
LOCATION:Magick Oak - Metaphysical Center & Enchanted Goods
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/tea-and-tarot-element-of-a
 ir-alchemy-of-thought?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260518T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260518T170000
UID:260501GUTs8UNU0k-cJxrq8dtDEw
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
