BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Auditions for Little Shop of Horrors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T210000
UID:2604280p_DR4s5-E6LOGt686JDbw
DESCRIPTION:Greetings Auditioners for the musical\, Little Shop of Horrors
 ! \\(Broadway Version\\) at Bay Are Stage Theatre on Broadway!  Join the f
 un and showcase your talent! Bay Area Stage Theatre invites talent from al
 l over the Bay Area\, to audition for Little Shop of Horrors \\(Broadway V
 ersion\\)\, the fantastical musical\, by Howard Ashman \\(Book & Lyrics\\)
  and Alan Menken \\(Music\\). Directed at Bay Area Stage Theatre\, by Jeff
  Lowe and Musically Directed by Brian Sennello ATTENTION PLEASE: The previ
 ous audition notices for Little Shop were lost when our original page "Bay
  Area Stage Theatre" was hacked. Please sign up on the Zeffy event if you 
 didn't before\, so we have your contact info! https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/
 ticketing/auditions-little-shop-of-horrors-at-bay-area-stage-theatre We ar
 e dedicated to connecting our community through the arts. Be part of somet
 hing special and help us bring engaging performances to life. Location: Ba
 y Area Stage Theatre.  Date: May 23\, 24\, 25 7PM to 9PM.  Arrive at 7PM. 
 No individually timed appointments needed. 1\\) Please select the date of 
 your requested audition directly on Zeffy -  https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/t
 icketing/auditions-little-shop-of-horrors-at-bay-area-stage-theatre 2\\) P
 lease come prepared with physical sheet music in your key \\(preferred\\) 
 and/or a Youtube link to the track of your audition song or a copy on USB.
  No a capella. No vocal accompaniment on audition track. 3\\) Please have 
 your audition song memorized. 4\\) Dress for easy\, yet active movement. 5
 \\) No monologues are required. Cold Read from libretto. 6\\) Rehearsals b
 egin: August 2\, 2026 and are Monday through Thursday from 7PM to 10PM Tec
 h Week Begins: Saturday\, September 26 7\\) SHOW DATES: October 2\, 3\, 4\
 , 9\, 10\, 11\, 16\, 17\, 18\, 23\, 24\, 25 - 2026 Friday's and Saturday's
  at 8PM and Sunday matinees at 3PM Principal Characters These are the core
  storytelling roles: Seymour Krelborn – Meek\, insecure floral assistant
 \; the protagonist Audrey – Bleach-blonde shop girl with low self-esteem
 \; Seymour’s love interest Mr. Mushnik – Owner of the failing flower s
 hop\; Seymour’s boss/adoptive father figure Orin Scrivello\, D.D.S. – 
 Sadistic dentist\; Audrey’s abusive boyfriend Audrey II \\(The Plant\\) 
 – Carnivorous alien plant \\(puppet \\+ voice actor\\) Featured Trio \\(
 Greek Chorus\\) These roles are essential and are co-leads: Crystal Ronnet
 te Chiffon ➡️ Street urchins / doo-wop trio who: Narrate the story Fun
 ction as a Greek chorus Provide major vocal backbone of the score Featured
  Supporting / Doubling Roles Often played by ensemble actors doubling mult
 iple parts: Customers & Walk-ons First Customer Second Customer Mrs. Luce 
 – High-society client Skip Snip – Flower shop buyer \\(often comic cam
 eo\\) Radio / Media Voices WINK Radio Announcer / Interviewer Bernstein 
 – Business agent/producer type Minor Named Roles Patrick Martin – \\(o
 ptional/incidental\, depending on version\\) Ensemble \\(Flexible / Doubli
 ng Tracks\\) The ensemble fills out Skid Row and provides transitions\, mu
 sical support\, and incidental characters. Typical ensemble tracks include
 : Street People / Skid Row Residents Bums / Drifters Shop Customers \\(var
 ious\\) Dentist Patients \\(in “Dentist!” sequence\\) Reporters / Pres
 s Agents / Businessmen Neighborhood passersby ➡️ The ensemble often co
 vers and doubles many of the incidental speaking roles listed above. We lo
 ok forward to seeing you on stage. Sorry\, guys\, but my contract specifie
 s: No AEA
LOCATION:Bay Area Stage Theatre on Broadway
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2328001111040574/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
