SUMMARY:The California Honeydrops | Cookout Concert Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T180000
UID:260325hh7SWB8btkmsDMHn6AqBYw
DESCRIPTION:KC TURNER PRESENTS  THE CALIFORNIA HONEYDROPS BottleRock After
 Dark 13th Annual COOKOUT CONCERT SERIES HOPMONK NOVATO OUTDOOR VENUE Spons
 ored by JAMBAR MOSTLY STANDING ON GROUND LEVEL LIMITED SEATING ON LAWN & T
 OP OF HILL ALL AGES ABOUT: “The California Honeydrops...evoke the greasy
  rumble of Booker T and channel the spiritual ecstasy of Sly and the Famil
 y Stone.” -Rolling Stone Formed in the subway systems of Oakland\, retro
 -soul outfit The California Honeydrops are an electrifying group that defy
  convention at every turn. They’ve become a mainstay at festivals includ
 ing Byron Bay Bluesfest \\(Australia\\)\, Outside Lands\, Monterey Jazz\, 
 Lightning In A Bottle\, and touring with B.B. King\, Dr. John\, Bonnie Rai
 tt\, Buddy Guy\, and Allen Toussaint. Led by the enigmatic and energetic f
 rontman\, Lech Wierzynski\, and percussionist Benjamin Malament\, each mem
 ber of the band is a virtuoso in their own rite — Yanos “Johnny Bones
 ” Lustig on saxophone\, Lorenzo Loera on keyboards/guitar\, Beaumont Bea
 ullieu on drums\, Miles Blackwell on bass\, and regularly accompanied by O
 liver Tuttle on trombone\, Leon Cotter on saxophone/clarinet\, and Miles L
 yons on trombone/sousaphone — navigating through a vast repertoire of or
 iginal songs and timeless classics every night. But what truly sets them a
 part is their unwavering commitment to the art of improvisation - a skill 
 so finely honed that they have completely abandoned the use of set lists a
 nd no two shows are ever the same. Off stage\, their music has been stream
 ed more than 200 million times\, and placed in a variety of TV and films\,
  including “Dead To Me\,” “Alaska Daily\,” “Black-ish” and mor
 e. Their new album “Redwood Highway” was released August 8\, 2025. ---
 -------------------------------- EVENT INFO: Q: Is this show outdoors? A: 
 Yes. This event is held in HopMonk Novato's outdoor concert venue. Q: Are 
 kids allowed? A: The shows are all ages. Kids need a ticket to attend. No 
 babies in arms. Q: Is there seating? A: Seating is limited and is first co
 me. You're allowed a LOW-BACK chair in the lawn section. At the top of the
  hillside section there is table seating that is first come. We recommend 
 arriving at the time doors open. Some shows are open dance floor/standing 
 room only while others are mostly seated. Varies from show to show. Q: Is 
 there parking? A: Parking is free and there is plenty of it. NO PETS NO CO
 OLERS NO BACKPACKS NO OUTSIDE FOOD NO UMBRELLAS NO REFUNDS | ALL SALES FIN
 AL Tickets: After completing your purchase on See Tickets\, you will recei
 ve an email confirmation with your attached PDF ticket\\(s\\). You MUST pr
 int and bring your PDF tickets AND VALID PHOTO IDENTIFICATION to be admitt
 ed for the event. You may download the See Tickets app and show your ticke
 t on your mobile device for entry in lieu of printing.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1724454618531426/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T170000
UID:260501FKt9reKBDECJf4T2qWkPqg
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
